<title>FRANCE: French consumer prices rose 0.3 pct in January.</title>
<headline>French consumer prices rose 0.3 pct in January.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following final data:</p>
<p>				    Jan	  Dec	 Jan 1996</p>
<p> Month-on-month inflation   0.3	  0.2	  0.2</p>
<p> Year-on-year inflation     1.8	  1.7	  2.0</p>
<p> CPI Index (base 1990)    114.7	114.4	112.7</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following breakdown of the consumer price index for all households in mainland France, base 1990.</p>
<p>     Category		  Weight(pct) index  1-mo   3-mo  yr/yr</p>
<p> Food excluding tobacco	 20.20    109.1   1.6    2.3    2.5</p>
<p> Private-sector manufactures  32.77    107.4  -1.1   -1.6    0.0</p>
<p> Private-sector services	19.64    125.7   0.4    0.6    1.8</p>
<p> Energy				8.66    115.8   0.8    1.5    6.1</p>
<p> Public services ex energy     6.46    129.5   1.4    2.3    2.9</p>
<p> Rent, water			 6.68    129.9   0.2    0.4    2.2</p>
<p> Health spending		   5.59    110.1  -0.1    0.0    0.9</p>
<p> Total excluding tobacco	98.02    113.6   0.2    0.2    1.6</p>
<p>NOTE - INSEE said preliminary inflation figures are never given for January. It said the weightings for the different components of the index had changed. Base year (1990) remains unchanged.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom 331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
